1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,500
Music

2
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:17,640
The economist Eli Cook has studied how money has become the measure of everything in society.

3
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:26,260
And in an article in The Atlantic in 2017 titled How Money Became the Measure of All Progress,

4
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:34,200
he outlines how in the mid-19th century in America, everything started to be put in economic terms,

5
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:41,220
all development, all social welfare measures, and soon this became adopted right around the world.

6
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:45,720
He closes his article with a powerful statement.

7
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:46,740
He says,

8
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:55,660
By making capital accumulation synonymous with progress, money-based metrics have turned human betterment into a secondary concern.

9
00:00:56,260 --> 00:01:01,820
By the early 21st century, American society's top priority became its bottom line,

10
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:04,720
net worth became synonymous with self-worth,

11
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:10,260
and a billionaire businessman who repeatedly pointed to his own wealth

12
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:14,540
as proof of his fitness for office was elected president.

13
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:20,580
In recent decades, another phenomenon took hold, the digital revolution.

14
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:28,940
And with the advent of smartphones in 2010, literally, the universe landed in the palm of our hands.

15
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:37,620
And very soon, we were incapable of carrying out even our daily tasks without constantly accessing them.

16
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:43,220
From ordering groceries to our banking systems, they became our lifeline.

17
00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:49,000
And smartphones have become our closest and most cherished relationships,

18
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:54,420
just evidenced by the number of times we access it, nearly 100 on average,

19
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:57,200
and the number of hours we look at them,

20
00:01:57,580 --> 00:02:00,540
and the fierceness with which we protect their possession.

21
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:06,240
So this phenomenon of money becoming the measure of everything

22
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:10,460
was given a rocket fuel with the digital revolution.

23
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:12,340
And before we knew it,

24
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,740
countries, companies, and institutions started to out-compete each other

25
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:22,900
in pursuit of a mythical techno-commercial nirvana.

26
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:31,720
This has brought us to an unsustainable point as a society with three distinct but interrelated trends.

27
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:35,980
The first, steadily deteriorating human well-being.

28
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:39,100
And for the first time in recorded history,

29
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:45,600
every successively younger generation is getting more and more impacted with their mental health.

30
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:54,700
With 18 to 24-year-olds being three to five times worse off than the oldest generation that's working today.

31
00:02:55,800 --> 00:03:02,140
Second, accelerating economic disparities with very few beneficiaries

32
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:05,480
and at the expense of the vast majority.

33
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:11,620
And third, a profound disaggregation of our sense of self

34
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:18,180
and our relationship with others, with the society, and with the planet we reside in.

35
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:22,760
Literally, everything that we seek for ourselves and our loved ones,

36
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,460
wealth, well-being, and peace,

37
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:31,480
is what we seem to be collectively destroying in our pursuit as a society.

38
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:37,920
I believe we need to make two distinct and fundamental shifts in the world.

39
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:43,940
First, we need to redefine success from success just being equal to money

40
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:47,100
to a four-fold definition of success.

41
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:51,920
Meaning, success for organizations, institutions, and countries

42
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:57,340
ought to be about first, being financially viable and fiscally responsible.

43
00:03:57,860 --> 00:04:01,520
Second, fostering a more inclusive society.

44
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:04,840
Third, creating a more sustainable planet.

45
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:11,680
And fourth, committing to human well-being for all that we serve.

46
00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:19,820
And the second shift is to make well-being a core purpose of organizations.

47
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:23,560
Meaning, through the pursuit of work or education,

48
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:27,040
people ought to gain in physical health.

49
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:31,240
Be mentally energized, be emotionally fulfilled,

50
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:35,920
and be spiritually grounded to the purpose that they are here for.

51
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:42,760
These ideas of redefining success and making well-being a core purpose

52
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:47,800
may sound utopian and fantastical, and they likely are.

53
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:53,020
Yet, we've come to a tipping point as a society,

54
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:55,080
and unless we make this leap,

55
00:04:55,080 --> 00:05:00,460
I truly believe we are not going to leave this planet in a better place for future generations.

56
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:03,740
So, I'm reaching out for the similarly inspired,

57
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:06,280
those that are working day in and day out

58
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:10,340
in making this planet, this society, the people

59
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:14,020
better for our future generations.

60
00:05:14,020 --> 00:05:22,220
I'm reaching out to scientists and economists and educators and artists and sports professionals.

61
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:26,880
Literally, every sphere of human endeavor.

62
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:30,540
I'm seeking to join our forces together

63
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:33,700
so collectively we can learn from each other

64
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:35,480
and support each other

65
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:38,480
and leave this planet in a better shape

66
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:41,140
for those that will follow behind us.

67
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:43,140
Thank you.

